rve a one-game suspension Saturday as part of the school's self-imposed penalties for impermissible contacting of players.","published":"2026-11-25T00:01:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586972/wyoming-coach-jay-sawvel-gets-self-imposed-1-game-suspension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 20 Florida shuts down WR Vernell Brown for season-ending knee surgery","description":"No. 20 Florida is shutting down receiver Vernell Brown III for the remainder of the season.","published":"2026-11-24T23:07:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586755/no-20-florida-shuts-wr-vernell-brown-season-ending-knee-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Viral couple from Wake Forest-Georgia Tech game speaks on 'Today' show","description":"The couple's intense discussion was caught on an ESPN broadcast of Wake Forest and Georgia Tech's Week 12 game and went viral.","published":"2026-11-24T21:02:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584732/wake-forest-georgia-tech-viral-couple-speaks","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado's Deion Sanders shrugs off hot-seat chatter before UCF","description":"Deion Sanders handles outside chatter -- in this case, speculation over his future as coach at Colorado -- by simply tuning out the noise.","published":"2026-11-24T21:29:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585728/colorado-sanders-shrugs-hot-seat-chatter-ucf","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Memphis' Charles Huff says he's not candidate for Maryland head coaching job","description":"Memphis' Charles Huff said he's not a candidate for the head coaching vacancy at Maryland and will not be part of this year's coaching carousel.","published":"2026-11-24T20:33:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585465/charles-huff-says-not-candidate-maryland-hc-job","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NCAA sanctions Liberty over tampering with two players before entering portal","description":"Among the penalties the NCAA announced against Liberty, two coaches and the GM received show-cause penalties over tampering.","published":"2026-11-24T20:05:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585093/ncaa-sanctions-liberty-transfer-portal-tampering","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star OT Lincoln Fa'alafi commits to Notre Dame, to join 2028 class","description":"New Zealand native Lincoln Fa'alafi, ESPN's No. 8 overall prospect in the 2028 cycle, committed Tuesday to Notre Dame.","published":"2026-11-24T19:56:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584881/notre-dame-gets-2028-commitment-ot-lincoln-faalafi","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A timeline of Michigan athletics since 2017","description":"Warde Manuel's eventful decade in Ann Arbor has been marked by athletic successes and marred by controversy.","published":"2026-11-24T18:47:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5218633/ryan-wingo","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Wingo"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ryan Wingo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Wingo","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:38Z","intro":"Ryan Wingo (born February 15, 2006) is an American college football wide receiver for the Texas Longhorns.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wingo attended St. Louis University High School in St. Louis, Missouri. During his high school career he had 129 receptions for 2,160 yards and 31 receiving touchdowns. Wingo played in the 2024 All-American Bowl. A five-star recruit, he committed to the University of Texas at Austin to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his first collegiate game as a true freshman in 2024, Wingo had four receptions for 70 yards. Wingo scored his first college touchdown against UTSA in Week 3. He played in all 16 games and ended the season with 472 receiving yards, 100 rushing yards, and 2 receiving touchdowns.\nIn his sophomore season in 2025, Wingo was named to the preseason All-SEC second team. He scored his first touchdown of the season in Week 3 against UTEP. In Week 4 against Sam Houston, Wingo logged 93 receiving yards, 32 rushing yards, and 2 touchdowns, making it his first game with multiple touchdowns. In Week 9 against Mississippi State, Wingo recorded a career-high 184 receiving yards on five receptions. At the end of the season, Wingo was named to the All-SEC second team."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Ronnie Wingo","description":"American football player","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ronnie_Wingo"}]}}